            <ArticleTitle>A rapidly growing coronary pseudoaneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>320-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2015.05.007</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(15)00140-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Little is known regarding the evolution of coronary aneurysms. We report on a rapidly growing coronary pseudoaneurysm with the aim to underline the reasons for rapid coronary aneurysm enlargement and the different therapeutics options available to face this rare clinical condition.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
